## Why This Is Asked
Tests at scale must validate multi-tenant data isolation, region-resident content, and flag-driven UX under outages. This probes orchestration, data management, and resilience.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenancy isolation and data residency
- Content personalization pipelines and identity graphs
- Feature flags and A/B test routing
- Regional outages and retry strategies
- Test data seeding and reproducibility

## Code Example
```javascript
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('e2e: multi-tenant personalization with feature flags', async ({ page }) => {
  const tenant = 'tenantA';
  await page.route('https://content.example.com/api/personalize', route =>
    route.fulfill({ status: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ banner: 'A', content: 'X' }) })
  );
  await page.goto(`https://content.example.com/${tenant}?region=eu`);
  await expect(page.locator('#banner')).toHaveText('A');
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate data isolation with real data vs. mock data across tenants?
- How do you scale tests across regions without flakiness and ensure coverage for outage scenarios?

